cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Reduced multiscale complexity of RR intervals in Parkinson's disease across acquisition modalities and recording lengths: code and derived data"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data for a multicohort study of RR-interval multiscale complexity
  in Parkinson's disease, combining short resting ECG (CETRAM, Santiago),
  photoplethysmography during resting-state fMRI (Hospital Universitario Cruces,
  Bilbao) and 24-hour ambulatory wearable chest-strap ECG (Nagoya University Hospital).
  Complexity is quantified by refined composite multiscale entropy (rcMSE) with a
  fixed tolerance, computed in Julia (with a Python port verified to machine
  precision); statistics and figures are in Python.
type: software
license: MIT
